<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.9: Aspire Admin Reviews and Submits Campaign for Cre=
ates Campaign Setup (Step-9)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an <strong>Admin</strong>, I want to review all configured phishing c=
ampaign settings in one consolidated summary page before submission, so tha=
t I can verify accuracy, make any necessary corrections, and confidently su=
bmit the campaign for execution.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>In the <strong>Review &amp; Submit</strong> step (final step of the camp=
aign creation wizard), the <strong>Admin</strong> is shown a structured sum=
mary of all previously configured campaign settings, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Setup</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Email Template</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Tags</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Audience</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Schedule</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p>Each section includes an <strong>Edit</strong> button, allowing the Admi=
n to return to the specific configuration step and make changes if needed.<=
/p>
<p>Once reviewed, the <strong>admin</strong> can select <strong>Submit Camp=
aign</strong>, after which the system validates all settings, finalizes cam=
paign scheduling, and queues or activates the campaign according to the def=
ined delivery method and frequency.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Reviews all settings, edits sections if needed, =
and submits the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the full campaign summary, validates c=
onfiguration, and processes the final submission.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> has completed all prior steps in the Cre=
ate Campaign wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>All mandatory fields in earlier steps are valid.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system can retrieve and display all campaign configuration data.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> is authenticated and authorized to creat=
e campaigns.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The campaign is successfully submitted and saved in the system.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The campaign status changes to&nbsp;<strong>Queued</strong>,&nbsp;<stron=
g>Scheduled</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Active</strong>, depending on the del=
ivery method.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> is redirected to the&nbsp;<strong>Campai=
gn List</strong> page where they can monitor progress.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Display Review Summary</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>System</strong> displays a complete read-only summary o=
f all configured campaign sections:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Setup</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Campaign Name:</p></li>
<li>
<p>Campaign Type: Simulated Phishing &amp; Security Awareness Training</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Email Template</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Language: English</p></li>
<li>
<p>Template Type: all</p></li>
<li>
<p>Selected Template: ID 3</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Language: Not selected</p></li>
<li>
<p>Template Type: Not selected</p></li>
<li>
<p>Selected Template: Not selected</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Selected Server: client-sendgrid</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Tags</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Assigned Tags: Q1, Q3</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Audience</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Audience Type: Predefined Groups</p></li>
<li>
<p>Target Count: 1 predefined group</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Training Language: English</p></li>
<li>
<p>Assignment Type: Assign All</p></li>
<li>
<p>Selected Modules: 1</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Schedule</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Delivery Method: Dec 02, 2025 =E2=80=93 Dec 05, 2025</p></li>
<li>
<p>Frequency: one-off</p></li>
<li>
<p>Time Zone: GMT+10:00</p></li>
<li>
<p>Expiry Date: Dec 03, 2025</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>For each section, the system displays the&nbsp;<strong>Edit</strong> but=
ton, allowing the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> to make adjustments if necess=
ary.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Admin Edits Configuration (Optional)</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> may click&nbsp;<strong>Edit</strong> on =
any section to modify the settings.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system navigates the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> back to the corresp=
onding step.</p></li>
<li>
<p>After saving changes, the system returns to the&nbsp;<strong>Review &amp=
; Submit</strong> step with the updated settings.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Submit Campaign</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>Admin</strong> clicks&nbsp;<strong>Submit Campaign</str=
ong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>System</strong> validates the following configurations:=
</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Delivery Method</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Frequency</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail Server</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Audience Selection</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Schedule</strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training Assignment (if applicable)</strong></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>System</strong> displays a confirmation message:<br>
"Your campaign is now being processed according to the configured schedule.=
"</p></li>
<li>
<p>The&nbsp;<strong>System</strong> redirects the&nbsp;<strong>Admin</stron=
g> to the&nbsp;<strong>Campaign List</strong> page where they can monitor t=
he campaign's progress.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>All required campaign settings must be complete</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Error: </strong>=E2=80=9CPlease complete all mandatory configura=
tion steps before submission.=E2=80=9D</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Schedule validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Must have valid delivery method, frequency, and start date.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Mail server must be selected</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Error: </strong>=E2=80=9CA valid mail server must be configured =
before submitting.=E2=80=9D</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Audience must contain at least one valid target</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Error: </strong>=E2=80=9CPlease select at least one audience gro=
up.=E2=80=9D</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"18=
a69f90-c30b-4131-a224-6124b5474a6b" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 74.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 685.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>BR-1</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>All required campaign configuration fields across all steps must be vali=
d before submission.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>BR-2</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must be able to edit any section from the <strong>Review</strong> =
page.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>BR-3</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Campaign cannot be submitted without a <strong>Mail Server</strong>.</p>=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>BR-4</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Campaign cannot be submitted if no <strong>Audience</strong> is selected=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>BR-5</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>System must save all final campaign settings before processing the campa=
ign.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"27=
a48c68-790d-4d0a-98ce-dd721d33bf1a" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 84.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 425.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 248.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select a <strong>Phishing Delivery Method</st=
rong> (Immediate or Scheduled).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Delivery method is selectable and works as expected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong=
> (One-off, Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency options are available and can be selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select a <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong=
> (optional).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Expiry date can be selected and displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-04</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can configure the <strong>First Batch Delivery</s=
trong> option, choosing between scheduled or immediate delivery.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>First batch delivery option works correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can enter a <strong>Test Email Address</strong> a=
nd send a test email.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Test email is sent successfully.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can select the <strong>Scheduled Delivery date an=
d time</strong> for emails.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Scheduled date and time are validated and displayed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-07</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system validates that all required fields (Delivery Method, Frequenc=
y) are completed before enabling the "Save &amp; Continue" button.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>"Save &amp; Continue" button is only enabled after completing required f=
ields.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-08</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can preview the scheduled campaign delivery in a =
confirmation message before finalizing.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Confirmation message is displayed with campaign details.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-09</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can send a <strong>Test Email</strong> to verify =
the campaign configuration.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Test email is received and matches the campaign setup.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-10</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can choose to <strong>Send Test Email</strong> be=
fore finalizing campaign setup.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Test email functionality works properly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-11</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> setting persists after saving.</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency setting remains saved and is available on subsequent views.</p=
></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-12</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can view the <strong>Expiry Date</strong> setting=
 and edit it if necessary.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Expiry date can be viewed and edited as needed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-13</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>First Batch Delivery</strong> can be set for a specific time and=
 date.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can choose to set the first batch delivery time a=
nd date.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-14</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Campaign Settings</strong> are saved successfully after clicking=
 <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Settings are saved and confirmed by the system.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-15</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can set the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> t=
o "One-off" for a single delivery.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>"One-off" option functions correctly for single campaign delivery.</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-16</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Test Email Delivery</strong> field is visible but optional.<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can choose to enable or skip test email delivery.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-17</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can <strong>Edit</strong> the <strong>Campaign Fr=
equency</strong> after the initial selection.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency field is editable and changes are saved correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-18</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Campaign Expiry Date</strong> can be removed if not needed.<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Expiry date can be cleared if not required.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-19</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> receives a confirmation notification when setting=
s are successfully saved.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Confirmation message is displayed after successful save.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>AC-20</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Admin</strong> can view the <strong>Campaign Frequency</strong> =
and <strong>Expiry Date</strong> settings in the campaign summary.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Frequency and expiry date settings are displayed in the summary.</p></td=
>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>System Behavior &amp; Validation</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The system retrieves all stored configuration values from previous steps=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p>All values displayed must be read-only except via Edit.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Validation runs once again at the point of final submission.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If scheduling is invalid, system blocks submission and highlights the is=
sue.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Security Handling</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Only&nbsp;<strong>authorized Admin roles</strong> can review and submit =
campaigns.</p></li>
<li>
<p>All sensitive configuration data (Mail Server credentials, template IDs,=
 schedule times) are&nbsp;<strong>encrypted at rest</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Unauthorized users cannot access or modify campaign settings.</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Aspire Admin, I want to review the entire phishing simulation camp=
aign configuration before final submission to ensure all settings are corre=
ct and that the campaign will be executed as planned.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>In Step 8 of the <strong>Create New Campaign</strong> wizard, the Aspire=
 Admin reviews all settings related to the phishing simulation campaign bef=
ore finalizing and submitting it for processing. This step includes reviewi=
ng the <strong>Campaign Overview</strong>, <strong>Email Configuration</str=
ong>, <strong>Target Audience</strong>, <strong>Training Configuration</str=
ong>, <strong>Landing Page Configuration</strong>, and <strong>Schedule &am=
p; Delivery Configuration</strong>. The Admin can edit any section if neede=
d, and once all details are verified, the Admin clicks the <strong>Submit C=
ampaign</strong> button to initiate the campaign execution. The system disp=
lays a confirmation message and the status of the campaign. The Admin can a=
lso monitor the campaign progress from the <strong>Campaign List</strong> p=
age after submission.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Aspire Admin</strong>: Reviews and verifies the configuration se=
ttings, edits sections if necessary, and submits the campaign.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the campaign summary, validates the se=
ttings, and submits the campaign.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Aspire Admin has completed all the previous steps in the <strong>Cre=
ate New Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system is operational and displays all campaign configuration settin=
gs in the <strong>Review</strong> section.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is logged in and has necessary privileges to submit the campai=
gn.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The campaign configuration is reviewed and finalized.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The campaign is submitted for execution, and the system processes the ca=
mpaign based on the selected settings.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The campaign will appear in the <strong>Campaign List</strong>, where th=
e Admin can track its progress.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Campaign Overview Review</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Aspire Admin is presented with the <strong>Campaign Overview</strong=
> section.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>This includes <strong>Campaign Name</strong> and <strong>Campaign Type</=
strong> (e.g., Simulated Phishing, Training).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Edit</strong> if any details need to be chan=
ged.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 2: Email Configuration Review</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the <strong>Email Configuration</strong> section:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Includes <strong>Email Template Language</strong> and <strong>Mail Serve=
r</strong> settings.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If needed, the Admin can click <strong>Edit</strong> to update the setti=
ngs.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 3: Target Audience Review</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the <strong>Target Audience</strong> section:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Displays <strong>Audience Type</strong> (Predefined Groups or Custom Gro=
ups) and <strong>Target Count</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the Admin wants to modify the target audience, they can click <strong=
>Edit</strong>.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 4: Training Configuration Review</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the <strong>Training Configuration</strong> section:</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Displays <strong>Training Language</strong>, <strong>Assignment Type</st=
rong>, and <strong>Selected Modules</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If any training modules or settings need to be adjusted, the Admin can c=
lick <strong>Edit</strong>.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 5: Landing Page Configuration Review</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the <strong>Landing Page Configuration</strong> sectio=
n:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Displays the selected <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> (e.g., Error/40=
4: Page Not Found, Custom Landing Page).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Edit</strong> to change the landing page typ=
e.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 6: Schedule &amp; Delivery Configuration Review</strong></p=
>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the <strong>Schedule &amp; Delivery Configuration</str=
ong> section:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Displays <strong>Delivery Method</strong> (Immediate or Scheduled), <str=
ong>Frequency</strong> (One-off, Weekly, Monthly, Quarterly), and <strong>C=
ampaign Expiry Date</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>If any changes are required, the Admin can click <strong>Edit</strong>.<=
/p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 7: Final Submission</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>After reviewing all sections and ensuring the campaign settings are corr=
ect, the Admin clicks <strong>Submit Campaign</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays a confirmation message: "Your campaign has been succ=
essfully submitted and will be processed according to the configured schedu=
le."</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Edit Configuration</strong> to make any fina=
l changes or <strong>Submit Campaign</strong> to finalize the campaign.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is redirected to the <strong>Campaign List</strong> page to mo=
nitor the campaign's progress.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Campaign Overview</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Campaign Name and Campaign Type.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: These fields must not be empty.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Campaign name and type are required."</=
p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Email Configuration</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Email Template Language and Mail Server.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: These fields must be valid and selected.</p=
></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please review email configuration setti=
ngs."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Target Audience</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Audience Type and Target Count.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: Audience group must be selected correctly.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a target audience."</p></=
li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Training Configuration</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Training Language and Assigned Modules.</p></=
li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: These fields must be configured.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select training modules."</p></l=
i>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page Configuration</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Landing Page Type.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: Ensure a valid landing page is selected.</p=
></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid landing page."</p=
></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Schedule &amp; Delivery Configuration</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Delivery Method, Campaign Frequency, and Camp=
aign Expiry Date.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: Ensure that all scheduling fields are compl=
eted.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please review the delivery schedule set=
tings."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
